<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Endovelicus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Endovelicus was a god of the pre-Roman peoples of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, worshipped above all at a sanctuary near Alandroal in Portugal's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a>. Dozens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> dedications from the Roman period, many by people with Roman names, thank him for health or answered prayers, suggesting a healing and oracular cult. He is one of the best-documented native deities of Lusitania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/endovelicus.jpg" alt="Endovelicus" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mike Steele · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portugal_National_Museum_of_Archaeology_(28691245028).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
